    "summary": "High‑energy Capitol show with smoking Morning Dew and epic Other One",
    "blurb": "The set delivers a scorching Morning Dew, a jaw‑dropping The Other One suite, and a breakneck Johnny B. Goode. Jerry’s Les Paul shines while Phil’s bass drives the jams, and Pigpen adds tasteful Hammond textures. Soundboard recordings capture the band’s tight, high‑energy performance throughout.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Capitol Theater on February 23 1971 finds the Dead in peak form, charging through a set that balances raw power with inspired improvisation. The first half roars with a smoking Morning Dew and a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, while the second set builds momentum into a landmark Drums → The Other One → Wharf Rat → Greatest Story Ever Told suite capped by an electrifying Johnny B. Goode. Jerry’s Les Paul tone cuts through the mix despite being slightly recessed, delivering staccato leads and soaring solos; Phil’s thumping bass sits front‑and‑center, anchoring every jam. Pigpen’s Hammond B‑3 adds subtle color, especially on the Bird Song, while Bill Kreutzmann’s punchy drumming propels the band forward even when a loose pedal moment shows up. With crystal‑clear soundboard sources that capture every nuance, this show stands out as one of the most exciting early‑’70s performances in the Dead catalog.",
